      "text": "To find 10% of 20% of a number, we first need to calculate 20% of a certain number.\n\nHint:\n12$^{\\mathrm{ th }}$ part of a number = 20% of 10% of that number = 20% × 10%\n\nSo, we need to find 10% of 20% of the number, which is 20% × 10% × the original number.\n\nGiven that 20% × 10% of a number is 12, we can said that 20% × 10% of the original number, should be 12.\n\nSo, 10% of 20% of the number should be equal to (20% × 10% × the original number) / 100.\n\nLet's denote the original number as x. Then, we can write:\n\n20% × 10% × x = 12\n\nNow, we can simplify this equation:\n\n0.2 × 0.1 × x = 12\n\n0.02x = 12\n\nTo find x, we divide both sides of the equation by 0.02:\n\nx = 12 / 0.02\n\nx = 600\n\nNow that we have the original number, we can find 10% of 20% of the number:\n\n10% × 20% × x = 10% × 20% × 600\n\n0.1 × 0.2 × 600 = 0.2 × 600\n\n= 120\n\nSo, 10% of 20% of the number is 120.",
